    "id": 545,
    "chapter": 7,
    "chapterTitle": "Pediatric Physiology and Anesthesia",
    "stem": "During surgery for correction of scoliosis, somatosensory evoked potential (SSEP) monitoring is employed. An increase in SSEP latency and a decrease in amplitude could be explained by each of the following EXCEPT",
